# Cloudflare Pages redirect map — DTLM Architect
#
# Brief §9.2: "Build a redirect map from old URLs to new... Losing project and
# press URLs means losing accumulated search ranking."
#
# STATUS (updated): the site was restructured from separate pages into a
# single scrollable homepage with anchor sections. This is a deliberate,
# client-confirmed departure from the 14 Aug 2026 decision recorded below to
# preserve the existing WordPress URL structure — SEO equity loss on the
# retired paths is an accepted tradeoff, softened with the 301s below rather
# than left as dead 404s.
#
# ORIGINAL DECISION (14 Aug 2026, now superseded for the paths listed):
# the client asked to preserve the existing WordPress URL structure rather
# than move to the /projects/ paths proposed in brief §4. That decision still
# stands for the pages that remain real routes: /accessibility/, /privacy/,
# /contact/thank-you/.
#
# WHAT STILL NEEDS DOING BEFORE LAUNCH
#
# 1. The WordPress news archive at /category/updates/ (and its paginated pages)
#    has no equivalent, because §5 Option 2 replaces the post archive with a
#    single curated section. Every individual post URL under it needs a
#    redirect. Those URLs are NOT yet known — see the Phase 0 audit.
#
# 2. Run a crawl of the live (old) site immediately before cutover and diff it
#    against the built site's sitemap. Anything indexed and not covered below
#    needs a line here.
#
# 3. Verify Cloudflare Pages' _redirects engine passes a #fragment through in
#    the Location header for a 301 (expected — it's a plain HTTP header, and
#    fragments are resolved client-side once the browser follows it — but not
#    yet confirmed against Cloudflare's specific handling). If it turns out
#    fragments get stripped, drop the #fragment from the rows below and
#    redirect to bare "/" instead.

# --- Retired standalone pages, folded into homepage anchor sections --------
/works/                        /                    301
/portfolio/*                   /#selected-works     301
/project-type/*                /#selected-works     301
/about/                        /                    301
/team/                         /                    301
/news/                         /#news               301
/contact/                      /#contact            301

# --- News archive -----------------------------------------------------------
# The archive index and its pagination collapse onto the News section.
/category/updates/            /#news   301
/category/updates/page/*      /#news   301

